1
00:00:21,700 --> 00:00:26,220
(Notice)
Welcome to an Immersive Life Simulation.

2
00:00:26,980 --> 00:00:33,140
Welcome to Door of Truth,
an open-world social deduction game.

3
00:00:33,140 --> 00:00:36,020
You will enter the dungeon world
as a player

4
00:00:36,020 --> 00:00:38,740
and begin your adventure.

5
00:00:38,960 --> 00:00:41,480
This game includes four cases.

6
00:00:42,120 --> 00:00:43,720
(Case 1, Case 2, Case 3, Case 4)
In each case,

7
00:00:43,720 --> 00:00:45,800
(Characters)
you will unlock a new character

8
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:47,920
and experience a different life path.

9
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:49,680
By exploring

10
00:00:49,680 --> 00:00:51,760
and interacting with NPCs,

11
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:54,880
you will uncover each story,

12
00:00:54,880 --> 00:00:56,000
solve the case,

13
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:57,480
and find the culprit.

14
00:00:57,480 --> 00:00:59,200
(Case 1, 2, 3, 4 completed)
Complete all cases

15
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:01,160
to earn the completion achievement

16
00:01:01,160 --> 00:01:02,800
(Completion Achievement)
and unlock the hidden ending.

17
00:01:03,280 --> 00:01:04,480
Each case

18
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:05,600
(Case 1, Case 2)
may contain one

19
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:07,160
or more investigations.

20
00:01:07,160 --> 00:01:08,400
(Random, Detective, Suspect)
When the case begins,

21
00:01:08,400 --> 00:01:10,400
you will be randomly assigned

22
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:11,360
as a detective or suspect.

23
00:01:11,880 --> 00:01:14,160
(Suspect, NPC)
The true culprit may be

24
00:01:14,160 --> 00:01:15,520
a suspect player or an NPC.

25
00:01:15,520 --> 00:01:17,400
(Culprit)
Choose carefully.

26
00:01:17,400 --> 00:01:19,240
The culprit's goal

27
00:01:19,240 --> 00:01:20,720
is to remain hidden.

28
00:01:20,720 --> 00:01:23,400
(Culprit)
Only the true culprit may lie.

29
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:24,760
(Main Quest, Clues, Exploration, Rewards)
During the game,

30
00:01:24,760 --> 00:01:27,200
(Skill Card, Trial, Stamina, Side Quest)
different mechanics

31
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:28,800
can be triggered to advance the case.

32
00:01:29,480 --> 00:01:30,800
Use them wisely

33
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:32,400
for an unexpected breakthrough.

34
00:01:33,720 --> 00:01:34,800
(Suspect, Culprit, NPC)
After the investigation,

35
00:01:34,800 --> 00:01:36,520
the culprit vote begins.

36
00:01:37,280 --> 00:01:38,680
If the culprit is identified,

37
00:01:38,680 --> 00:01:40,120
(Correct Vote, Culprit)
players who voted correctly

38
00:01:40,120 --> 00:01:42,200
receive a Golden Key.

39
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:43,840
If the player is the culprit

40
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:45,680
(Culprit, Players)
and receive fewer votes,

41
00:01:45,680 --> 00:01:48,200
(Culprit, Vote, Players)
that culprit earns a Golden Key.

42
00:01:48,920 --> 00:01:50,960
(Players)
Golden Keys are awarded

43
00:01:50,960 --> 00:01:52,560
after the case ends.

44
00:01:52,560 --> 00:01:54,920
(Skill Card)
They can be exchanged for Skill Cards.

45
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:56,860
(Notice)
Please confirm.

46
00:01:56,860 --> 00:01:58,840
(All descriptions are fictional.)
Notice

47
00:01:58,840 --> 00:02:00,650
(Settings and actions are setups.)
Dungeon world loading complete.

48
00:02:00,650 --> 00:02:02,690
(All photos and videos)
Please immerse yourselves

49
00:02:02,690 --> 00:02:04,010
(are authorized.)
in the experience.

50
00:02:04,010 --> 00:02:04,340
(Safety measures were taken
during shooting. Don't try this at home.)

51
00:02:04,340 --> 00:02:04,780
(Parental supervision required
for underage viewers.)

52
00:02:04,780 --> 00:02:05,860
(Loading)

53
00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:10,700
(Loading...)

54
00:02:10,700 --> 00:02:13,220
(Dungeon Pass)

55
00:02:18,060 --> 00:02:19,380
(The Truth)

56
00:02:20,420 --> 00:02:24,460
=The Truth (Season 4)=

57
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:25,760
Case 4.

58
00:02:25,760 --> 00:02:26,720
Crazy Animal Theme Party.

59
00:02:26,720 --> 00:02:27,760
The game glitched.

60
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:29,520
There's a bug!

61
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:29,840
What?

62
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:30,480
What bug?

63
00:02:32,880 --> 00:02:33,600
What's going on?

64
00:02:34,280 --> 00:02:35,040
What happened?

65
00:02:36,080 --> 00:02:36,680
How...

66
00:02:36,680 --> 00:02:37,880
How did we end up

67
00:02:37,880 --> 00:02:38,680
in the game lobby?

68
00:02:42,320 --> 00:02:42,680
He...

69
00:02:42,880 --> 00:02:44,120
You're...

70
00:02:44,120 --> 00:02:45,640
Designer Bai?

71
00:02:45,640 --> 00:02:46,560
I'm so sorry.

72
00:02:46,560 --> 00:02:48,160
Our game glitched again.

73
00:02:48,840 --> 00:02:50,440
Why are there so many bugs?

74
00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:51,760
I've created

75
00:02:51,760 --> 00:02:52,720
a temporary lounge.

76
00:02:52,720 --> 00:02:53,520
You can head over there

77
00:02:53,520 --> 00:02:54,480
and get some rest.

78
00:02:55,140 --> 00:02:56,540
(System maintenance. Players offline)

79
00:02:56,540 --> 00:02:57,460
(Server maintenance. Patching)

80
00:02:57,460 --> 00:02:58,670
(Maintenance complete. Server online)

81
00:02:58,690 --> 00:03:00,180
(Server starting soon)

82
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:01,920
(The system has been restored)
System restored.

83
00:03:02,360 --> 00:03:02,920
Please log back in.

84
00:03:03,080 --> 00:03:03,640
Let's go.

85
00:03:03,640 --> 00:03:05,280
(June 23, 10AM. Server Online)
Let's get back

86
00:03:05,280 --> 00:03:06,320
to our investigation.

87
00:03:06,320 --> 00:03:07,440
Okay.

88
00:03:07,440 --> 00:03:08,320
Let's go.

89
00:03:11,120 --> 00:03:11,760
Come on.

90
00:03:21,100 --> 00:03:22,020
(Dungeon launch failed)

91
00:03:22,140 --> 00:03:23,060
Ah!

92
00:03:23,060 --> 00:03:23,900
Open it now!

93
00:03:23,900 --> 00:03:25,260
Come on, come on!

94
00:03:25,260 --> 00:03:26,780
Group up! Group up!

95
00:03:26,780 --> 00:03:29,390
Guys, I think we hit another bug.

96
00:03:29,390 --> 00:03:31,930
(The newly fixed system bugged again)
The lighting system is broken.

97
00:03:32,350 --> 00:03:34,110
All that work for nothing.

98
00:03:35,080 --> 00:03:36,000
(Night vision mode)
I'll go check

99
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:36,680
what's wrong.

100
00:03:36,680 --> 00:03:37,440
Wait here.

101
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:39,860
Don't die.

102
00:03:39,860 --> 00:03:41,020
(Could it be you?)

103
00:03:41,100 --> 00:03:42,420
(Sneaking around)

104
00:03:43,500 --> 00:03:46,780
(OMG, you scared me!)

105
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:48,520
He's not any braver this season,

106
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:49,800
but he's gotten way sneakier.

107
00:03:52,760 --> 00:03:53,800
Smells so good.

108
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:55,280
How do you smell

109
00:03:55,280 --> 00:03:56,680
(Vision impaired, smell enhanced)
different every day?

110
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,400
(Original pun-style singing)
Let's answer with "smell".

111
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:01,280
If we keep hugging like this,

112
00:04:01,280 --> 00:04:02,280
we're gonna catch feelings.

113
00:04:02,280 --> 00:04:02,760
Seriously.

114
00:04:02,780 --> 00:04:04,240
(The darkness brought us together)
Suspension bridge effect.

115
00:04:04,760 --> 00:04:05,440
Seriously.

116
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:07,560
The teleport pod has arrived.

117
00:04:08,800 --> 00:04:09,360
What pod?

118
00:04:09,360 --> 00:04:11,060
(Teleport pod has arrived)

119
00:04:11,320 --> 00:04:13,200
The teleport pod has arrived.

120
00:04:13,200 --> 00:04:14,760
Are we getting teleported?

121
00:04:16,830 --> 00:04:17,560
What does that mean?

122
00:04:18,120 --> 00:04:19,440
Maybe someone just arrived.

123
00:04:19,440 --> 00:04:20,480
(Did someone get)
Or maybe someone's leaving.

124
00:04:20,480 --> 00:04:21,820
(teleported in or out?)

125
00:04:25,420 --> 00:04:26,900
(Lighting bug fixed)

126
00:04:26,920 --> 00:04:28,280
All fixed.

127
00:04:28,280 --> 00:04:29,240
What does that mean?

128
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:30,520
What does it mean?

129
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:32,360
It says the teleport pod has arrived.

130
00:04:32,360 --> 00:04:33,880
Should we go check it out?

131
00:04:33,880 --> 00:04:34,440
Let's go.

132
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:35,280
Let's head outside.

133
00:04:35,280 --> 00:04:36,120
Let's go check.

134
00:04:36,120 --> 00:04:36,640
Let's go.

135
00:04:39,340 --> 00:04:40,500
(Unknown area)

136
00:04:40,520 --> 00:04:41,880
Okay, go! Hurry!

137
00:04:42,840 --> 00:04:44,120
That's it, right?

138
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:44,520
Yeah.

139
00:04:44,520 --> 00:04:45,260
(The teleport pod)

140
00:04:53,640 --> 00:04:55,440
This is the return pod.

141
00:04:55,440 --> 00:04:56,120
No, it's the teleport pod.

142
00:04:56,600 --> 00:04:58,480
Case 1, Case 2,

143
00:04:58,480 --> 00:05:00,560
Case 3, Case 4.

144
00:05:06,460 --> 00:05:07,940
(Mission Hub.
The green border is the scanner)

145
00:05:07,940 --> 00:05:08,940
(Teleport Pod Dock, Game Archive)

146
00:05:08,960 --> 00:05:10,920
So this is the game archive.

147
00:05:11,060 --> 00:05:13,220
(Game Archive)

148
00:05:13,960 --> 00:05:15,840
Security scanning
is enhanced in this area.

149
00:05:15,840 --> 00:05:17,120
Any outside weapons, poisons,

150
00:05:17,120 --> 00:05:17,520
explosives,

151
00:05:17,520 --> 00:05:18,600
or offensive skill modules

152
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:19,520
cannot be brought inside.

153
00:05:19,580 --> 00:05:21,580
(No weapons allowed in this area)

154
00:05:21,600 --> 00:05:23,400
If dangerous external items

155
00:05:23,400 --> 00:05:24,600
are detected inside,

156
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:26,280
a continuous alarm will be triggered.

157
00:05:26,280 --> 00:05:28,840
If a player is killed in this area,

158
00:05:28,840 --> 00:05:31,000
it will directly
damage the player administrator's

159
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:31,680
consciousness data,

160
00:05:31,680 --> 00:05:34,080
causing them to become brain-dead

161
00:05:34,080 --> 00:05:35,560
in the real world.

162
00:05:35,580 --> 00:05:38,460
(Death here
means brain death in real life)

163
00:05:42,360 --> 00:05:42,960
I get it.

164
00:05:42,960 --> 00:05:45,080
So this is a game world.

165
00:05:45,080 --> 00:05:46,720
The players here

166
00:05:46,720 --> 00:05:47,680
were transported in.

167
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:49,080
But if you die

168
00:05:49,080 --> 00:05:49,720
in the game,

169
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:50,920
you die in real life too.

170
00:05:50,920 --> 00:05:51,980
(If a player dies in the game,)

171
00:05:51,980 --> 00:05:53,340
(their real-world body
becomes brain-dead)

172
00:05:53,360 --> 00:05:54,840
Got it.

173
00:05:55,500 --> 00:05:58,340
(The game world
and the real world are connected)

174
00:05:59,320 --> 00:06:01,480
This is the teleport pod entrance.

175
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:02,820
(Mission Hub.
The green border is the scanner)

176
00:06:02,820 --> 00:06:03,660
(Game Archive)

177
00:06:04,580 --> 00:06:06,500
(Teleport pod entrance location)

178
00:06:06,520 --> 00:06:07,160
This.

179
00:06:07,680 --> 00:06:08,840
This is the teleport pod.

180
00:06:09,640 --> 00:06:10,600
Double doors.

181
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:11,500
(Teleport pod entrance)

182
00:06:15,560 --> 00:06:16,680
There's a key.

183
00:06:18,160 --> 00:06:18,760
Here's a key.

184
00:06:18,760 --> 00:06:19,200
A key.

185
00:06:28,720 --> 00:06:30,120
Is this Designer Bai?

186
00:06:31,680 --> 00:06:32,880
The Truth Online reminds you.

187
00:06:33,400 --> 00:06:35,080
The game admin, Designer Bai,

188
00:06:35,080 --> 00:06:36,400
died unexpectedly.

189
00:06:36,400 --> 00:06:39,000
The game world's exit
is temporarily closed.

190
00:06:41,360 --> 00:06:44,320
Please find out how Designer Bai died

191
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:46,520
and find a way back to the real world.

192
00:06:46,520 --> 00:06:49,620
(Case 9: He Is Loading)

193
00:06:49,700 --> 00:06:50,820
(Current Case Summary)

194
00:06:50,820 --> 00:06:51,580
(Victim: Designer Bai)

195
00:06:51,580 --> 00:06:52,540
(Location of death:
Inside the teleport pod)

196
00:06:53,840 --> 00:06:54,280
Oh no.

197
00:06:54,920 --> 00:06:56,440
I told him to be careful.

198
00:06:56,880 --> 00:06:58,720
He was killed inside the teleport pod.

199
00:06:59,040 --> 00:07:00,960
So he got killed in real life too.

200
00:07:01,060 --> 00:07:02,160
(Designer Bai died in the game.
Brain-dead in the real world)

201
00:07:02,160 --> 00:07:03,400
He designed this game

202
00:07:03,400 --> 00:07:04,920
and ended up killing himself with it.

203
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:07,040
Wait. There's writing.

204
00:07:07,040 --> 00:07:08,600
It says "he".

205
00:07:08,880 --> 00:07:09,800
He is...

206
00:07:10,280 --> 00:07:12,040
(Designer Bai left a message)
It's a hexagram.

207
00:07:12,040 --> 00:07:13,680
That's our symbol.

208
00:07:14,880 --> 00:07:15,720
Over here. Look.

209
00:07:18,480 --> 00:07:19,120
(Night vision mode)
Don't do that.

210
00:07:19,120 --> 00:07:19,840
Someone's here.

211
00:07:19,840 --> 00:07:20,680
Seriously, stop.

212
00:07:20,680 --> 00:07:21,880
It's okay. I'll protect you.

213
00:07:21,880 --> 00:07:22,280
Don't do that.

214
00:07:23,200 --> 00:07:24,000
I've got a big sword.

215
00:07:24,680 --> 00:07:25,200
Come on.

216
00:07:25,200 --> 00:07:25,960
I'm here.

217
00:07:29,820 --> 00:07:30,900
(New player joined)

218
00:07:31,100 --> 00:07:31,800
(Who's there?)

219
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:32,360
Hello.

220
00:07:32,760 --> 00:07:33,480
Everyone,

221
00:07:33,480 --> 00:07:35,560
I'm an investigator from the real world.

222
00:07:35,760 --> 00:07:37,040
(Not part of the game world)
Real-world investigator.

223
00:07:37,040 --> 00:07:37,520
Hello.

224
00:07:37,920 --> 00:07:39,480
(Investigator, played by Zhou Jinglin)
Time is running out.

225
00:07:39,480 --> 00:07:41,080
I can only log into the game
for two minutes.

226
00:07:41,080 --> 00:07:42,840
After two minutes, I'll log out.

227
00:07:43,240 --> 00:07:43,640
Okay.

228
00:07:43,640 --> 00:07:44,320
Then hurry.

229
00:07:44,320 --> 00:07:46,400
Our agency has been investigating

230
00:07:46,400 --> 00:07:47,400
a hacker.

231
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:49,200
His codename is "Loading".

232
00:07:49,200 --> 00:07:50,200
Loading.

233
00:07:50,200 --> 00:07:51,600
He's been using the internet

234
00:07:51,600 --> 00:07:53,400
to commit many crimes.

235
00:07:53,800 --> 00:07:56,360
(Loading committed multiple cybercrimes)
We've been tracking him.

236
00:07:56,360 --> 00:07:58,680
We've now identified some of his traits.

237
00:07:58,960 --> 00:08:00,120
Take a look.

238
00:08:00,120 --> 00:08:00,400
Okay.

239
00:08:01,640 --> 00:08:02,760
Suspect sketch.

240
00:08:02,760 --> 00:08:03,560
Codename, Loading.

241
00:08:03,960 --> 00:08:05,200
(Suspect Sketch)
Gender, male.

242
00:08:05,640 --> 00:08:06,680
Occupation, hacker.

243
00:08:06,680 --> 00:08:07,400
Criminal record.

244
00:08:07,400 --> 00:08:09,160
Used hacking to commit multiple crimes.

245
00:08:09,480 --> 00:08:10,320
After every crime,

246
00:08:10,320 --> 00:08:12,400
he leaves behind
a "Loading Complete" card.

247
00:08:12,400 --> 00:08:13,600
Confirmed traits.

248
00:08:13,600 --> 00:08:15,280
Protects his left shoulder.

249
00:08:15,880 --> 00:08:16,720
Seems to be injured.

250
00:08:16,720 --> 00:08:17,600
Possibly injured.

251
00:08:17,600 --> 00:08:19,840
Burn scar on the back of his right hand.

252
00:08:19,840 --> 00:08:20,200
A scar.

253
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:21,880
IP address traced.

254
00:08:21,880 --> 00:08:23,520
777 Happiness Road.

255
00:08:24,040 --> 00:08:25,600
The suspect

256
00:08:25,600 --> 00:08:26,760
has strong counter-surveillance skills.

257
00:08:26,760 --> 00:08:27,560
His digital footprints

258
00:08:27,560 --> 00:08:29,280
are usually erased within 12 hours

259
00:08:29,280 --> 00:08:30,720
after each crime.

260
00:08:31,320 --> 00:08:35,240
This address is the only one
he ever failed to erase.

261
00:08:35,550 --> 00:08:36,640
So he's a wanted criminal.

262
00:08:37,240 --> 00:08:38,600
A professional hacker.

263
00:08:38,600 --> 00:08:39,080
A hacker.

264
00:08:39,400 --> 00:08:39,760
Come on.

265
00:08:39,760 --> 00:08:41,720
(Check his arm)
See if he has it.

266
00:08:42,760 --> 00:08:43,400
We've got our suspect.

267
00:08:43,400 --> 00:08:44,480
Oh no.

268
00:08:44,480 --> 00:08:45,080
He's the guy.

269
00:08:45,080 --> 00:08:45,920
What do you mean?

270
00:08:45,920 --> 00:08:46,760
(Matching him)
You're the guy.

271
00:08:48,080 --> 00:08:50,080
So this hacker is the killer?

272
00:08:50,080 --> 00:08:52,180
(Did Loading kill Designer Bai?)

273
00:08:52,200 --> 00:08:52,880
Didn't he draw

274
00:08:52,880 --> 00:08:53,680
something on his arm?

275
00:08:53,680 --> 00:08:54,580
(Designer Bai's message on his arm)
He wrote "he is".

276
00:08:54,580 --> 00:08:55,040
(Hinting at Loading)
It means

277
00:08:55,040 --> 00:08:56,080
Loading killed him.

278
00:08:56,080 --> 00:08:56,240
Right.

279
00:08:57,080 --> 00:08:58,160
The killer is Loading.

280
00:08:58,220 --> 00:08:59,100
(Current Case Summary
Victim: Designer Bai)

281
00:08:59,100 --> 00:09:00,120
(Location of death: Inside the teleport pod
