00:23:06,960 --> 00:23:07,960
ended up in us.

832
00:23:07,960 --> 00:23:08,320
Yeah.

833
00:23:08,920 --> 00:23:10,480
(Missing me again)
He shaped part of who we are.

834
00:23:10,480 --> 00:23:11,680
He made us who we are.

835
00:23:14,280 --> 00:23:16,120
So what did I inherit?

836
00:23:16,120 --> 00:23:16,920
Brains.

837
00:23:17,560 --> 00:23:18,000
Seriously?

838
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:18,360
Yeah.

839
00:23:20,480 --> 00:23:22,320
(Teleportation complete)
Memory Gate unlocked.

840
00:23:22,320 --> 00:23:23,640
Players, please exit the pods.

841
00:23:24,240 --> 00:23:25,940
(Pod 1)
Memory Gate unlocked.

842
00:23:25,960 --> 00:23:26,320
Come on.

843
00:23:29,520 --> 00:23:30,840
This is way too dark.

844
00:23:30,860 --> 00:23:32,420
(Night vision mode)

845
00:23:32,420 --> 00:23:34,860
(This fictional story
contains horror elements)

846
00:23:34,880 --> 00:23:35,920
I don't scare easily,

847
00:23:35,920 --> 00:23:37,440
but even I'm a little freaked out.

848
00:23:37,440 --> 00:23:38,960
(Says she's scared,
but she's already charging ahead)

849
00:23:38,960 --> 00:23:40,460
(We need Longdong Army)
Longdong Army!

850
00:23:40,460 --> 00:23:41,940
(to protect us now)
Longdong Army!

851
00:23:41,940 --> 00:23:47,000
Longdong Army!

852
00:23:49,160 --> 00:23:49,840
This is so dark.

853
00:23:53,260 --> 00:23:53,860
(Longdong Army protection activated)

854
00:23:53,860 --> 00:23:54,380
(Ah!)

855
00:23:58,160 --> 00:24:00,000
(Cheng has become fearless)
You scared me.

856
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:00,580
(Getting braver)

857
00:24:01,040 --> 00:24:02,360
Girls,

858
00:24:02,360 --> 00:24:03,120
stop pulling on my clothes.

859
00:24:03,120 --> 00:24:04,520
(Keep those shoulders covered)
Sorry.

860
00:24:04,520 --> 00:24:05,560
(Sorry, girl)

861
00:24:05,560 --> 00:24:06,280
Girls,

862
00:24:06,280 --> 00:24:07,600
detectives, go!

863
00:24:07,600 --> 00:24:08,480
I'm scared!

864
00:24:08,480 --> 00:24:09,240
(Detectives are powerless this round)
I'm here.

865
00:24:09,240 --> 00:24:09,680
Let's go.

866
00:24:09,920 --> 00:24:10,720
Let's go.

867
00:24:10,720 --> 00:24:12,220
(Mountain ahead, shield behind)

868
00:24:12,220 --> 00:24:13,100
(Protecting detectives at all costs)

869
00:24:15,640 --> 00:24:16,520
It's okay.

870
00:24:16,580 --> 00:24:17,520
(Shield comes with a calming effect)

871
00:24:17,520 --> 00:24:18,760
I'm right behind you, okay?

872
00:24:19,560 --> 00:24:20,840
What does it look like?

873
00:24:20,840 --> 00:24:21,680
(Scared, but way too curious)
Let me take a look.

874
00:24:23,400 --> 00:24:24,640
It'll open again.

875
00:24:24,640 --> 00:24:26,000
When it comes out, we'll scream at it.

876
00:24:26,000 --> 00:24:26,640
Okay.

877
00:24:28,340 --> 00:24:29,620
(Launching a magical attack)

878
00:24:29,640 --> 00:24:30,680
Are we just

879
00:24:30,680 --> 00:24:31,960
going in circles?

880
00:24:32,300 --> 00:24:35,020
(Wandering through a complicated
memory space)

881
00:24:35,040 --> 00:24:35,720
Ding, you go first.

882
00:24:35,980 --> 00:24:38,020
(Newly appointed point man)

883
00:24:39,300 --> 00:24:40,380
(Shield charges ahead,
mountain guards the rear)

884
00:24:40,400 --> 00:24:41,960
Hold onto me. I'm scared.

885
00:24:41,980 --> 00:24:43,320
(Detectives still need protection)
It's okay. We're right behind you.

886
00:24:43,320 --> 00:24:44,080
Ning and I are behind you.

887
00:24:44,080 --> 00:24:45,280
(Leading the way with his eyes closed)

888
00:24:45,280 --> 00:24:47,200
You're walking a little slow, Ding.

889
00:24:47,800 --> 00:24:48,680
I'll go first.

890
00:24:48,680 --> 00:24:50,000
Ding, you good?

891
00:24:50,120 --> 00:24:50,840
Come on! Go!

892
00:24:51,440 --> 00:24:51,880
What?

893
00:24:51,880 --> 00:24:52,880
(Who are you underestimating?)

894
00:24:52,880 --> 00:24:53,320
Watch this.

895
00:24:53,600 --> 00:24:54,440
There!

896
00:24:54,440 --> 00:24:55,200
It's getting brighter!

897
00:24:59,800 --> 00:25:00,520
This is a kitchen.

898
00:25:00,960 --> 00:25:01,680
They're making crepes.

899
00:25:02,720 --> 00:25:03,480
Time to eat!

900
00:25:04,240 --> 00:25:04,880
Smells amazing!

901
00:25:04,880 --> 00:25:06,700
(Memory fragment 1 unlocked)

902
00:25:08,320 --> 00:25:09,040
Come on, eat.

903
00:25:09,680 --> 00:25:11,400
(Do not touch the griddle. Hot surface)
They actually make crepes here.

904
00:25:11,880 --> 00:25:12,880
Who's most afraid of this?

905
00:25:12,880 --> 00:25:15,440
Who's most afraid of these high-calorie crepes?

906
00:25:15,440 --> 00:25:16,600
Crepes.

907
00:25:16,600 --> 00:25:18,420
(Whose memory fragment is this?)

908
00:25:18,760 --> 00:25:19,320
Let's eat.

909
00:25:19,320 --> 00:25:20,640
(Might as well eat while we're here)

910
00:25:20,640 --> 00:25:21,600
Here, I'll do it.

911
00:25:21,600 --> 00:25:22,240
(Chef Liu takes over the kitchen)
You know how to make these?

912
00:25:22,240 --> 00:25:22,640
I do.

913
00:25:22,640 --> 00:25:24,000
Seriously, Ning?

914
00:25:24,000 --> 00:25:25,360
(National Level 3 Culinary Certificate)
Ning, you're incredible!

915
00:25:25,360 --> 00:25:26,000
(Master of Northeast Chinese
home cooking)

916
00:25:26,000 --> 00:25:26,660
(Years of kitchen experience.)
I can make all this.

917
00:25:26,660 --> 00:25:27,320
(Can handle anything in the kitchen)
What's so hard?

918
00:25:27,380 --> 00:25:29,100
(Too skilled to play it cool)

919
00:25:29,700 --> 00:25:31,380
(Crepes now available)

920
00:25:31,760 --> 00:25:33,360
Don't we need this?

921
00:25:33,360 --> 00:25:33,960
The oil brush?

922
00:25:33,960 --> 00:25:35,120
Fry the sausages first.

923
00:25:35,120 --> 00:25:36,100
(Assigning
an assistant to prep the toppings)

924
00:25:37,040 --> 00:25:37,560
See?

925
00:25:37,560 --> 00:25:39,480
This is what happens when you
put a chef in a place like this.

926
00:25:39,480 --> 00:25:40,560
They just know what to do.

927
00:25:40,560 --> 00:25:41,360
No one has to tell them.

928
00:25:41,360 --> 00:25:42,380
(Pure muscle memory)

929
00:25:42,600 --> 00:25:43,840
How many are we feeding?

930
00:25:43,840 --> 00:25:44,320
One, two, three, four...

931
00:25:44,320 --> 00:25:45,200
Six people.

932
00:25:45,200 --> 00:25:45,560
Here.

933
00:25:45,940 --> 00:25:47,140
(Manual turntable)

934
00:25:47,480 --> 00:25:47,800
Okay.

935
00:25:47,800 --> 00:25:48,520
Now the eggs.

936
00:25:49,920 --> 00:25:50,440
Good.

937
00:25:54,120 --> 00:25:54,560
Perfect.

938
00:25:55,380 --> 00:25:56,340
(Drawn in by the smell)

939
00:25:57,120 --> 00:25:57,800
Ning.

940
00:25:57,800 --> 00:25:59,840
Smells amazing, Ning!

941
00:25:59,840 --> 00:26:00,720
Yeah.

942
00:26:00,720 --> 00:26:01,840
We need to scrape it off.

943
00:26:01,860 --> 00:26:02,900
(Every Saturday at noon:
Door of Truth Player Extras)

944
00:26:02,900 --> 00:26:03,840
(Catching more hilarious player moments)

945
00:26:03,840 --> 00:26:05,320
But we didn't oil it earlier.

946
00:26:05,320 --> 00:26:05,960
(A traditional flatbread griddle)
Right. We didn't oil it.

947
00:26:05,960 --> 00:26:06,880
(Can't let go of the griddle)
We didn't oil it.

948
00:26:07,720 --> 00:26:08,880
Oh no.

949
00:26:09,240 --> 00:26:09,920
It's okay.

950
00:26:10,120 --> 00:26:11,800
Try again.

951
00:26:11,800 --> 00:26:13,200
I think I know what went wrong.

952
00:26:13,200 --> 00:26:13,920
There we go.

953
00:26:13,920 --> 00:26:14,560
Perfect.

954
00:26:17,720 --> 00:26:18,200
Have some of this.

955
00:26:18,200 --> 00:26:18,640
I'll eat it in a minute.

956
00:26:18,640 --> 00:26:19,280
This is so good.

957
00:26:19,280 --> 00:26:20,440
(Oil-free crepes,
great for weight loss)

958
00:26:20,440 --> 00:26:21,800
I think this one's really good too.

959
00:26:21,800 --> 00:26:22,640
(This is exactly my kind of food)
This is so good.

960
00:26:22,640 --> 00:26:23,520
So crispy.

961
00:26:26,460 --> 00:26:28,220
(The crepe master
keeps making the next one)

962
00:26:28,240 --> 00:26:28,520
Okay.

963
00:26:28,520 --> 00:26:29,880
I'll flip this one.

964
00:26:32,140 --> 00:26:34,340
(Takes over topping duty)

965
00:26:37,000 --> 00:26:37,800
It's about to burn.

966
00:26:37,800 --> 00:26:38,880
Come grab it.

967
00:26:39,260 --> 00:26:40,700
(The crepe isn't ready yet.
Have some sides for now)

968
00:26:43,240 --> 00:26:43,960
Here.

969
00:26:43,960 --> 00:26:44,560
(Ding has officially
become the apprentice)

970
00:26:44,560 --> 00:26:45,040
Spread more.

971
00:26:45,040 --> 00:26:45,840
(#CrepeMasterpiece)

972
00:26:45,840 --> 00:26:46,880
Yeah, spread it out more.

973
00:26:46,880 --> 00:26:47,980
(Learning
from experience and starting over)

974
00:26:48,440 --> 00:26:49,480
Got it. Nice!

975
00:26:49,480 --> 00:26:50,400
Here, help me turn it.

976
00:26:50,400 --> 00:26:51,940
(Teaching with plenty of encouragement)

977
00:26:51,940 --> 00:26:54,180
(Ning-style crepe recipe:
use just enough batter)

978
00:26:54,180 --> 00:26:55,120
(Spreading the batter in a circle)

979
00:26:55,120 --> 00:26:55,400
Egg.

980
00:26:56,060 --> 00:26:57,660
(Jin cracks an egg one-handed.)
Good. One more. Crack another.

981
00:26:57,660 --> 00:26:59,980
(Spread egg evenly over the crepe)

982
00:27:00,520 --> 00:27:01,200
This one's perfect.

983
00:27:02,720 --> 00:27:03,400
Alright, come on.

984
00:27:03,400 --> 00:27:03,800
Turn it.

985
00:27:03,800 --> 00:27:04,400
It's fine. Just turn it.

986
00:27:05,180 --> 00:27:06,540
(Even the oil-brushed version
wants a taste test)

987
00:27:08,040 --> 00:27:08,240
That's it.

988
00:27:08,960 --> 00:27:10,360
This one's perfect!

989
00:27:10,420 --> 00:27:11,500
(Big and round)

990
00:27:11,640 --> 00:27:13,240
Ning, have you

991
00:27:13,240 --> 00:27:14,080
done this before?

992
00:27:14,080 --> 00:27:14,680
Never.

993
00:27:18,760 --> 00:27:20,240
But you even know how to flip it.

994
00:27:20,240 --> 00:27:21,320
That's impressive.

995
00:27:21,320 --> 00:27:22,680
You're a pro, Ning.

996
00:27:23,600 --> 00:27:24,200
Okay, go easy on the sauce.

997
00:27:24,200 --> 00:27:25,080
This stuff's really salty.

998
00:27:25,620 --> 00:27:28,100
(Keeping flavor and health in balance)

999
00:27:28,120 --> 00:27:28,560
Okay.

1000
00:27:29,160 --> 00:27:32,000
Alright, here we go.

1001
00:27:32,000 --> 00:27:32,640
Okay, that'll work.

1002
00:27:32,780 --> 00:27:33,280
(Flip the crepe and cook both sides.
Add toppings to taste)

1003
00:27:33,280 --> 00:27:34,160
(Ning-style crepes)
Alright, add another chicken tender.

1004
00:27:34,160 --> 00:27:35,720
(Eggs, sausage, ham, and chicken added)
Going all-out with the deluxe version.

1005
00:27:36,200 --> 00:27:36,840
20-something?

1006
00:27:37,020 --> 00:27:37,640
(Haggling over 20+)

1007
00:27:37,640 --> 00:27:38,200
This is

1008
00:27:38,200 --> 00:27:39,000
at least 20.

1009
00:27:39,000 --> 00:27:39,160
Right.

1010
00:27:39,420 --> 00:27:40,600
(Official price: 20)

1011
00:27:40,600 --> 00:27:41,200
Cut it up.

1012
00:27:41,200 --> 00:27:42,040
Cut it.

1013
00:27:42,520 --> 00:27:44,080
(Thoughtfully served)
Where do you find a guy like this?

1014
00:27:44,860 --> 00:27:46,760
If you're gonna marry anyone, marry.

1015
00:27:46,760 --> 00:27:50,060
Liu Yuning!

1016
00:27:51,000 --> 00:27:51,960
This looks so good.

1017
00:27:51,960 --> 00:27:52,560
(Instant craving)

1018
00:27:52,560 --> 00:27:53,760
Sprinkle some green onions on top.

1019
00:27:54,200 --> 00:27:54,480
Right?

1020
00:27:54,480 --> 00:27:56,260
(Green onions
added for the finishing touch)

1021
00:27:56,660 --> 00:27:58,520
(Order served)
Whose nightmare is this?

1022
00:27:58,520 --> 00:27:59,880
Who's scared of carbs, guys?

1023
00:28:00,040 --> 00:28:01,800
Who's the biggest foodie here?

1024
00:28:08,560 --> 00:28:09,640
So good.

1025
00:28:09,640 --> 00:28:10,160
Is it good?

1026
00:28:10,600 --> 00:28:11,200
It's amazing.

1027
00:28:11,200 --> 00:28:12,040
(Everyone's a foodie)

1028
00:28:12,040 --> 00:28:12,640
This is insanely good.

1029
00:28:13,080 --> 00:28:13,880
How's your hand?

1030
00:28:15,600 --> 00:28:16,480
It's fine now.

1031
00:28:17,200 --> 00:28:17,960
Make another one.

1032
00:28:17,960 --> 00:28:18,760
(A miracle worker)

1033
00:28:18,760 --> 00:28:19,400
Make another one.

1034
00:28:19,400 --> 00:28:20,320
Yeah, I'll make another.

1035
00:28:20,320 --> 00:28:21,040
It's fine. Won't take long.

1036
00:28:21,440 --> 00:28:22,840
I thought the first one was good too.

1037
00:28:22,840 --> 00:28:24,420
(We'll eat as many as you make)

1038
00:28:31,760 --> 00:28:32,360
Excuse me.

1039
00:28:34,160 --> 00:28:34,560
Excuse me.

1040
00:28:36,500 --> 00:28:37,500
(Who are you?)

1041
00:28:38,000 --> 00:28:38,560
Hello.

1042
00:28:39,200 --> 00:28:40,280
Are you guys

1043
00:28:40,280 --> 00:28:41,560
the staff?

1044
00:28:41,760 --> 00:28:42,360
Yeah.

1045
00:28:42,360 --> 00:28:43,120
(Naturally slipping
into their staff roles)

1046
00:28:43,120 --> 00:28:43,760
What can we do for you?

1047
00:28:43,760 --> 00:28:44,840
Do you know what time it is?

1048
00:28:44,840 --> 00:28:46,560
Shouldn't you guys be serving breakfast?

1049
00:28:46,560 --> 00:28:46,880
Wait.

1050
00:28:46,880 --> 00:28:49,000
(This memory needs a real restaurant)
Why are you eating the food?

1051
00:28:49,440 --> 00:28:50,760
(Claims the head chef position)
We serve breakfast?

1052
00:28:50,760 --> 00:28:52,800
(Claims the assistant chef position)
Wait, are we playing Overcooked?

1053
00:28:52,960 --> 00:28:53,960
Alright, sir. What do you want?

1054
00:28:53,960 --> 00:28:54,560
We'll make it for you.

1055
00:28:55,040 --> 00:28:56,200
Alright, I'll order.

1056
00:28:56,840 --> 00:28:57,720
I want...

1057
00:28:58,820 --> 00:28:59,580
(Customer, go ahead)

1058
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:01,720
Yo, yo, check it out!

1059
00:29:01,720 --> 00:29:03,440
One crepe, please.

1060
00:29:03,440 --> 00:29:05,440
Listen up, kid.

1061
00:29:05,440 --> 00:29:06,960
I'll tell you what I want,
and you make it.

1062
00:29:06,960 --> 00:29:07,440
Got it?

1063
00:29:07,700 --> 00:29:08,980
(Claims the order taker role)

1064
00:29:09,000 --> 00:29:10,480
Four eggs and one crispy crepe.

1065
00:29:10,480 --> 00:29:11,240
(Customer 1: Crepe)
Cut it in half.

1066
00:29:11,240 --> 00:29:12,680
(Quantity: 1)
Bean sauce that's not too sweet or salty.

1067
00:29:12,680 --> 00:29:14,080
(Special instructions)
Easy on the green onions.

1068
00:29:14,080 --> 00:29:16,320
One crepe, please!

1069
00:29:16,320 --> 00:29:18,000
If you don't want green onions,
what do you want?

1070
00:29:18,000 --> 00:29:19,000
(Already forgetting the order)

1071
00:29:19,400 --> 00:29:20,320
Four eggs!

1072
00:29:20,320 --> 00:29:22,120
Not too many.
Go easy on the green onions.

1073
00:29:22,120 --> 00:29:23,440
Go easy on the green onions.

1074
00:29:23,440 --> 00:29:24,360
(Everyone's accents are falling apart.)
Just a little.

1075
00:29:24,360 --> 00:29:25,680
Go easy on the green onions.

1076
00:29:25,680 --> 00:29:26,160
I...

1077
00:29:26,160 --> 00:29:29,280
(Every Friday at 12PM)
I just love my hometown's crepes.

1078
00:29:29,280 --> 00:29:31,160
(for more behind-the-scenes moments)
So good. Add some sesame seeds too.

1079
00:29:31,160 --> 00:29:32,260
(Even so good needs more flavor)

1080
00:29:33,380 --> 00:29:35,260
(Customer 1's order is ready)

1081
00:29:35,280 --> 00:29:36,160
This is actually pretty good.

1082
00:29:36,160 --> 00:29:37,000
Alright.

1083
00:29:37,000 --> 00:29:37,920
Here, take a glove.

1084
00:29:37,920 --> 00:29:38,600
Don't burn yourself.

1085
00:29:38,600 --> 00:29:39,640
Let me try it.

1086
00:29:39,640 --> 00:29:40,600
That's really thoughtful.

1087
00:29:40,600 --> 00:29:40,920
Yeah.

1088
00:29:40,920 --> 00:29:42,100
(Claims the waiter role)

1089
00:29:42,640 --> 00:29:43,000
Pay up.

1090
00:29:43,000 --> 00:29:44,080
Pay first.

1091
00:29:45,080 --> 00:29:47,360
Are these authentic Tianjin crepes?

1092
00:29:47,360 --> 00:29:48,520
We eat first.

1093
00:29:48,520 --> 00:29:50,280
(Claims the cashier role)
Authentic or not, you still gotta pay.

1094
00:29:50,840 --> 00:29:52,160
Who made this?

1095
00:29:52,360 --> 00:29:53,200
Chef Ning.

1096
00:29:53,580 --> 00:29:54,240
(Chef Ning proudly smirks)

1097
00:29:54,240 --> 00:29:55,040
Chef Ning?

1098
00:29:55,200 --> 00:29:55,920
That's right.

1099
00:29:56,560 --> 00:29:57,920
I used to be the head chef

1100
00:29:57,920 --> 00:30:00,400
at a three-Michelin-star restaurant in Dandong.

1101
00:30:00,500 --> 00:30:03,500
(Tui City Michelin)

1102
00:30:04,100 --> 00:30:07,780
(Let's see how it tastes)

1103
00:30:08,200 --> 00:30:08,800
It's good.

1104
00:30:11,200 --> 00:30:11,880
This one...

1105
00:30:12,460 --> 00:30:13,290
(Five-star customer review)

1106
00:30:13,290 --> 00:30:14,560
(So impressed, the customer
writes a 5,000-word review)

1107
00:30:14,560 --> 00:30:15,980
(Customer is moved to tears)

1108
00:30:17,080 --> 00:30:18,800
This tastes awful.

1109
00:30:18,980 --> 00:30:19,820
(Customer review)

1110
00:30:19,820 --> 00:30:20,780
(Ignore him. That's a bad review)

1111
00:30:22,740 --> 00:30:24,380
(Manually leaving a bad review)

1112
00:30:24,400 --> 00:30:24,960
Your crepe

1113
00:30:25,120 --> 00:30:26,040
isn't balanced.

1114
00:30:26,680 --> 00:30:28,920
It's not sweet enough or salty enough.

1115
00:30:29,360 --> 00:30:30,000
One star!

1116
00:30:30,000 --> 00:30:31,400
Didn't you say you wanted the sauce

1117
00:30:31,400 --> 00:30:33,240
neither sweet nor salty?

1118
00:30:33,480 --> 00:30:34,680
Balance!

1119
00:30:35,000 --> 00:30:36,200
Balance!

1120
00:30:36,460 --> 00:30:37,740
(You're getting a bad review too)

1121
00:30:38,800 --> 00:30:39,720
Balance.

1122
00:30:39,780 --> 00:30:41,740
(Back to the dining area)

1123
00:30:44,580 --> 00:30:46,180
(Another customer?)

1124
00:30:47,240 --> 00:30:48,760
Hey, can I get a crepe?

1125
00:30:48,760 --> 00:30:50,560
(Customer 2: Crepe, quantity unknown)
One of everything, no green onions.

1126
00:30:50,560 --> 00:30:51,880
(Special instructions: No green onions)
No green onions.

1127
00:30:51,880 --> 00:30:53,480
One order with...

1128
00:30:53,480 --> 00:30:54,120
Uh...

1129
00:30:54,120 --> 00:30:54,880
With... whatever... but not...

1130
00:30:56,440 --> 00:30:57,520
Want...

1131
00:30:57,720 --> 00:30:58,600
Three orders.

1132
00:30:58,600 --> 00:31:00,200
One order with everything
except green onions.

1133
00:31:00,200 --> 00:31:01,160
(Trying to memorize the order)
One order with everything except...

1134
00:31:01,160 --> 00:31:01,860
Crispy cracker, no lettuce.

1135
00:31:01,860 --> 00:31:02,430
Eggs, no spicy gluten strips.

1136
00:31:02,430 --> 00:31:02,980
Ham sausage, no sweet bean sauce.

1137
00:31:04,360 --> 00:31:07,640
Do you even know what you're saying?

1138
00:31:07,640 --> 00:31:09,360
You don't even know what you're saying!

1139
00:31:09,360 --> 00:31:09,960
Say it again.

1140
00:31:09,960 --> 00:31:10,600
Crispy cracker, no lettuce.

1141
00:31:10,600 --> 00:31:11,080
(Customer 2)
Eggs, no spicy gluten strips.

1142
00:31:11,080 --> 00:31:11,840
Ham sausage, no sweet bean sauce.

1143
00:31:11,840 --> 00:31:12,400
Got it.

1144
00:31:12,400 --> 00:31:13,400
Ham. Ham sausage.

1145
00:31:13,400 --> 00:31:14,160
(I know what you mean)
Got it.

1146
00:31:14,160 --> 00:31:15,680
I've noticed something
about the way you talk.

1147
00:31:15,680 --> 00:31:16,640
Why are you always...

1148
00:31:18,120 --> 00:31:19,120
Why do you always do that?

1149
00:31:19,600 --> 00:31:21,840
Yeah, your attitude sucks.

1150
00:31:22,320 --> 00:31:23,960
Our attitude's great.

1151
00:31:23,960 --> 00:31:25,080
One star.

1152
00:31:25,180 --> 00:31:26,580
(One disagreement
and it's an instant bad review.)

1153
00:31:26,800 --> 00:31:27,880
Hey, handsome.

1154
00:31:27,880 --> 00:31:28,400
Give you a one-star review.

1155
00:31:28,680 --> 00:31:29,760
What did you make?

1156
00:31:29,760 --> 00:31:30,620
(Customer gets mad.
The chef takes the blame)

1157
00:31:31,040 --> 00:31:32,640
Sorry to bother you!

1158
00:31:34,080 --> 00:31:34,680
Alright.

1159
00:31:34,680 --> 00:31:35,120
What would you like?

1160
00:31:35,120 --> 00:31:36,720
I want two orders of crepes.

1161
00:31:36,720 --> 00:31:37,480
Cook one

1162
00:31:37,480 --> 00:31:39,920
(Customer 3: 2 crepes)
until it's lightly golden.

1163
00:31:39,920 --> 00:31:42,080
(Special instructions)
Just a little crispy and browned.

1164
00:31:42,080 --> 00:31:42,840
Nice and fragrant.

1165
00:31:42,840 --> 00:31:44,840
The other one, don't brown it at all.

1166
00:31:44,840 --> 00:31:47,040
I want it soft and pale.

1167
00:31:47,040 --> 00:31:48,440
And...

1168
00:31:48,440 --> 00:31:50,720
The one with cilantro,
no crispy cracker.

1169
00:31:50,720 --> 00:31:52,240
The one with crispy cracker,

1170
00:31:52,240 --> 00:31:53,360
no egg.

1171
00:31:53,360 --> 00:31:55,360
(Forced smile)
Spicy gluten strips, add pork.

1172
00:31:55,360 --> 00:31:56,400
Make it fast.

1173
00:31:56,400 --> 00:31:56,880
Got it.

1174
00:31:56,880 --> 00:31:58,160
I just like my food hot.

1175
00:31:59,340 --> 00:32:06,140
(Trying not to laugh, cry, or lose it)

1176
00:32:06,220 --> 00:32:08,980
(Orders waiting to be made)

1177
00:32:09,000 --> 00:32:09,800
Here's what we're gonna do, Ning.

1178
00:32:09,800 --> 00:32:10,600
Just make him whatever.

1179
00:32:10,600 --> 00:32:12,600
He won't even remember what he ordered.

1180
00:32:12,600 --> 00:32:13,840
(Quietly doing the exact opposite)
That's the idea. Right.

1181
00:32:13,840 --> 00:32:16,860
(Time for the kitchen crew to get to work)

1182
00:32:17,420 --> 00:32:18,200
(Customer 2's order in progress)

1183
00:32:18,200 --> 00:32:18,760
Is this right?

1184
00:32:19,160 --> 00:32:19,400
That's enough.

1185
00:32:19,940 --> 00:32:21,700
(Customer 3's order in progress)

1186
00:32:27,920 --> 00:32:28,960
(A complete mess)
That looks awful.

1187
00:32:31,140 --> 00:32:32,740
(Adding extra egg to cover the mistakes)

1188
00:32:33,580 --> 00:32:34,980
(Still a complete mess)

1189
00:32:36,020 --> 00:32:37,460
(Giving up on presentation and serving it anyway)

1190
00:32:37,480 --> 00:32:39,560
These are all leftovers from other customers!

1191
00:32:40,360 --> 00:32:41,520
(Questionable hygiene)
Clear this out.

1192
00:32:41,520 --> 00:32:42,320
Seriously.

1193
00:32:42,320 --> 00:32:43,760
It's hard not to give them a bad review.

1194
00:32:43,920 --> 00:32:44,720
The atmosphere here

1195
00:32:44,720 --> 00:32:46,000
is terrible.

1196
00:32:46,220 --> 00:32:48,340
(We'll clean it up right away)

1197
00:32:51,820 --> 00:32:53,800
(Hygiene standards restored)
Too slow.

1198
00:32:53,800 --> 00:32:56,000
(Another complaint.)
Where's the other order? Hurry up!

1199
00:32:56,740 --> 00:32:58,140
(Limited kitchen capacity.
Can't go any faster)

1200
00:32:58,720 --> 00:32:59,720
Here, have some spicy gluten strips first.

1201
00:32:59,720 --> 00:33:00,900
(Trying to keep the customer happy)
These are actually good.

1202
00:33:02,840 --> 00:33:04,000
There's no real food.

1203
00:33:04,000 --> 00:33:05,040
We're just eating spicy strips?

1204
00:33:05,840 --> 00:33:07,000
My stomach...

1205
00:33:08,600 --> 00:33:10,440
That'll mess him up.

1206
00:33:11,400 --> 00:33:11,920
Nice.

1207
00:33:11,920 --> 00:33:12,760
Here.

1208
00:33:13,520 --> 00:33:14,800
Load it up.

1209
00:33:16,140 --> 00:33:18,700
(Small kitchen, generous portions)

1210
00:33:19,340 --> 00:33:22,220
(No one minds doing the dirty work)

1211
00:33:22,440 --> 00:33:22,840
Wait.

1212
00:33:22,840 --> 00:33:24,360
Give them some crispy crackers first.

1213
00:33:24,380 --> 00:33:25,980
(Crispy crackers first, crepes later.)

1214
00:33:26,440 --> 00:33:27,880
This is tiny.

1215
00:33:27,880 --> 00:33:28,600
Is this mine?

1216
00:33:28,600 --> 00:33:28,880
What...

1217
00:33:29,160 --> 00:33:29,760
What is this?

1218
00:33:29,760 --> 00:33:31,000
It's an appetizer.

1219
00:33:31,220 --> 00:33:32,680
(Appetizer:
Chef Ning's Michelin special)

1220
00:33:32,680 --> 00:33:33,320
An appetizer?

1221
00:33:33,320 --> 00:33:35,280
This is taking forever.

1222
00:33:36,760 --> 00:33:37,960
I can't watch this anymore.

1223
00:33:37,960 --> 00:33:39,080
Nope.

1224
00:33:39,880 --> 00:33:40,200
I'm in a hurry.

1225
00:33:40,200 --> 00:33:40,760
Forget it.

1226
00:33:40,760 --> 00:33:41,440
Let's go.

1227
00:33:41,440 --> 00:33:42,520
(No pressure, just crepes)
Forget it.

1228
00:33:42,520 --> 00:33:42,880
I...

1229
00:33:42,880 --> 00:33:43,760
But...

1230
00:33:44,280 --> 00:33:44,760
No way.

1231
00:33:44,760 --> 00:33:45,200
That's not happening.

1232
00:33:45,200 --> 00:33:46,600
(Nothing but bad reviews.)
Nope.

1233
00:33:46,600 --> 00:33:47,320
Serve the next one.

1234
00:33:47,320 --> 00:33:49,000
Cut one order into seven pieces.

1235
00:33:49,100 --> 00:33:49,920
(Customer scores a grilled cold noodle)

1236
00:33:49,920 --> 00:33:50,120
Right.

1237
00:33:50,120 --> 00:33:51,080
Just serve him one piece.

1238
00:33:51,440 --> 00:33:52,640
Coming up!

1239
00:33:53,960 --> 00:33:55,360
Whose crepe is this?

1240
00:33:56,160 --> 00:33:57,400
I don't even want it anymore.

1241
00:33:57,400 --> 00:33:58,080
I'm in a hurry.

1242
00:33:58,080 --> 00:33:59,120
Let's go.

1243
00:33:59,120 --> 00:34:01,320
You show up whenever
you want and leave whenever you want!

1244
00:34:01,320 --> 00:34:03,960
At least finish it before you leave!

1245
00:34:03,960 --> 00:34:05,240
I'm never coming back!

1246
00:34:05,240 --> 00:34:07,520
I'm reporting you to the manager!

1247
00:34:07,520 --> 00:34:08,600
No way!

1248
00:34:09,480 --> 00:34:10,360
Great. More for us.

1249
00:34:10,360 --> 00:34:11,080
(Good food stays in the family)
This is so good.

1250
00:34:11,080 --> 00:34:11,670
Awesome.

1251
00:34:11,670 --> 00:34:12,800
Wait.

1252
00:34:12,800 --> 00:34:14,080
He hasn't even eaten this one.

1253
00:34:14,080 --> 00:34:15,440
(Are we really eating this?)
Oh no. We made him

1254
00:34:15,440 --> 00:34:16,600
the deluxe version.

1255
00:34:16,600 --> 00:34:17,800
(Extra spicy, extra numbing)
Come on, we'll eat it. I'll eat it.

1256
00:34:17,800 --> 00:34:19,320
How are you going to eat that?

1257
00:34:22,440 --> 00:34:23,520
The chili smells amazing.

1258
00:34:24,600 --> 00:34:25,560
You take the spicy one.

1259
00:34:25,560 --> 00:34:25,880
I'll eat it.

1260
00:34:25,880 --> 00:34:26,980
(Food must not go to waste)
I love spicy food.

1261
00:34:27,580 --> 00:34:29,060
(The previous crepe has been claimed)

1262
00:34:31,840 --> 00:34:34,040
One star.

1263
00:34:34,040 --> 00:34:35,760
Another whole day's work for nothing.

1264
00:34:36,190 --> 00:34:36,670
What?

1265
00:34:37,710 --> 00:34:39,920
One star.

1266
00:34:39,920 --> 00:34:41,480
Another whole day's work for nothing.

1267
00:34:42,400 --> 00:34:43,710
Is that your voice?

1268
00:34:44,040 --> 00:34:45,440
Yours?

1269
00:34:45,760 --> 00:34:47,190
He's Loading.

1270
00:34:47,780 --> 00:34:51,100
(This is He's memory fragment)

1271
00:34:51,320 --> 00:34:52,080
What was that?

1272
00:34:52,280 --> 00:34:52,670
Wait.

1273
00:34:52,670 --> 00:34:53,400
What's that sound?

1274
00:34:54,710 --> 00:34:56,280
The drawer opened.

1275
00:34:58,600 --> 00:35:00,520
My shoulder hurts so bad again.

1276
00:35:00,520 --> 00:35:01,760
I can't even lift my arm.

1277
00:35:02,200 --> 00:35:02,840
Shoulder?

1278
00:35:02,840 --> 00:35:04,000
A patch on his left shoulder?

1279
00:35:04,000 --> 00:35:05,400
Does his shoulder hurt?

1280
00:35:05,400 --> 00:35:06,500
(Suspect Sketch)

1281
00:35:06,500 --> 00:35:08,340
(Guarding left shoulder, suspected injury.
Shoulder hurts again. Matches.)

1282
00:35:08,560 --> 00:35:10,440
One minute before off-time,

1283
00:35:10,440 --> 00:35:11,200
and I get saddled

1284
00:35:11,320 --> 00:35:13,280
with kneading a huge bucket
of dough again.

1285
00:35:13,280 --> 00:35:14,000
Stop zoning out.

1286
00:35:14,280 --> 00:35:16,520
Are you thinking about face-planting
into the flour again

1287
00:35:16,520 --> 00:35:17,200
to end all this?

1288
00:35:17,200 --> 00:35:18,960
Good job. You didn't do it.

1289
00:35:18,960 --> 00:35:19,880
This is the right hand.

1290
00:35:20,440 --> 00:35:21,080
A burn.

1291
00:35:21,080 --> 00:35:21,640
A right-hand burn.

1292
00:35:22,120 --> 00:35:22,640
Take a look.

1293
00:35:23,780 --> 00:35:24,940
(Physical feature: Burn scar on the back
of the right hand. Matches.)

1294
00:35:24,960 --> 00:35:25,600
That's terrifying.

1295
00:35:25,920 --> 00:35:28,520
February. Happy 20th birthday to me.

1296
00:35:28,520 --> 00:35:30,080
Lately I've been working part-time
at the crepe stand.

1297
00:35:30,080 --> 00:35:32,080
Mr. Wang always picks on me.

1298
00:35:32,080 --> 00:35:34,280
He makes me scrub the griddle
until midnight

1299
00:35:34,280 --> 00:35:35,880
and even makes me flip the crepes
with my bare hands.

1300
00:35:35,880 --> 00:35:38,200
My right hand
hit the 200-degree griddle.

1301
00:35:38,200 --> 00:35:39,680
Mr. Wang just said it won't kill me,

1302
00:35:39,680 --> 00:35:40,760
docked three days of my pay,

1303
00:35:40,760 --> 00:35:42,240
and spent 19 bucks on burn cream.

1304
00:35:42,800 --> 00:35:44,920
Applied the ointment for days,
and it still won't heal.

1305
00:35:44,920 --> 00:35:46,160
My classmate said
this is workplace bullying.

1306
00:35:46,600 --> 00:35:47,840
My classmate said
this is workplace bullying.

1307
00:35:47,840 --> 00:35:50,020
(He: Suspected victim
of workplace bullying)

1308
00:35:52,080 --> 00:35:53,320
And then, what else can I do?

1309
00:35:53,320 --> 00:35:54,840
If I don't work part-time,
I can't pay my tuition

1310
00:35:54,840 --> 00:35:56,160
and stay in Computer Science.

1311
00:35:56,760 --> 00:35:58,560
Computer Science.

1312
00:35:58,720 --> 00:35:59,840
It's definitely you.

1313
00:36:00,640 --> 00:36:02,160
This hand is totally yours.

1314
00:36:02,160 --> 00:36:02,800
Yeah.

1315
00:36:03,840 --> 00:36:04,560
It looks so much like it.

1316
00:36:04,560 --> 00:36:05,240
This is your hand.

1317
00:36:05,240 --> 00:36:06,320
It is your hand.

1318
00:36:06,320 --> 00:36:07,400
This is your hand.

1319
00:36:07,400 --> 00:36:08,800
This is 100% your hand.

1320
00:36:08,800 --> 00:36:10,760
This thumb is identical.

1321
00:36:11,060 --> 00:36:12,900
(He: Suspected to be Loading)

1322
00:36:13,480 --> 00:36:14,000
Here.

1323
00:36:14,320 --> 00:36:14,600
Meds.

1324
00:36:14,600 --> 00:36:15,360
"Don't Make a Fuss".

1325
00:36:15,360 --> 00:36:16,340
(Don't Make a Fuss)

1326
00:36:16,340 --> 00:36:17,260
(For traumatic anxiety and depression)

1327
00:36:17,260 --> 00:36:19,420
(For treating anxiety and depression)

1328
00:36:19,440 --> 00:36:21,120
You must be dealing
with some anxiety and depression.

1329
00:36:21,620 --> 00:36:23,460
(He has a mental illness?)

1330
00:36:23,720 --> 00:36:24,760
I really have no idea.

1331
00:36:25,200 --> 00:36:26,720
(Innocent)
I really don't know anything.

1332
00:36:26,720 --> 00:36:28,600
I really have no idea.

1333
00:36:30,360 --> 00:36:31,440
There's nothing left in the drawer.

1334
00:36:32,120 --> 00:36:33,080
There's more.

1335
00:36:33,280 --> 00:36:33,760
Really?

1336
00:36:33,840 --> 00:36:35,280
There's one more thing here.

1337
00:36:37,560 --> 00:36:37,960
Here.

1338
00:36:41,640 --> 00:36:42,120
He mentioned it.

1339
00:36:42,120 --> 00:36:44,040
(We Who Became Heirs)
He said that in the future he wanted

1340
00:36:44,040 --> 00:36:45,480
to create a dungeon like this
in a game world.

1341
00:36:45,480 --> 00:36:47,580
(Game script?)

1342
00:36:48,040 --> 00:36:50,680
In this dreamlike world,

1343
00:36:50,680 --> 00:36:51,680
everyone is born

1344
00:36:51,680 --> 00:36:54,440
as an heir to a top-tier family.

1345
00:36:54,440 --> 00:36:55,880
The instant coffee in the fridge

1346
00:36:55,880 --> 00:36:56,800
never runs out.

1347
00:36:58,520 --> 00:37:00,120
When shopping for designer bags,

1348
00:37:00,120 --> 00:37:01,360
you don't even check the price tag

1349
00:37:01,360 --> 00:37:03,000
before having the clerk
pull them down for you.

1350
00:37:03,800 --> 00:37:05,480
When dining at fancy restaurants,

1351
00:37:05,480 --> 00:37:06,560
you don't need to unpack

1352
00:37:06,560 --> 00:37:07,840
the disposable cutlery by yourself.

1353
00:37:07,840 --> 00:37:09,360
Most importantly,
going to work every day

1354
00:37:09,360 --> 00:37:11,360
is just to announce
that everyone has the day off today,

1355
00:37:11,360 --> 00:37:13,520
and then casually
pull down the shop shutters

1356
00:37:14,120 --> 00:37:15,840
to say goodbye to work.

1357
00:37:15,840 --> 00:37:17,040
So this title written on here,

1358
00:37:17,040 --> 00:37:18,440
"We Who Became Heirs",

1359
00:37:18,440 --> 00:37:19,520
must be his dream.

1360
00:37:19,760 --> 00:37:21,480
(We Who Became Heirs)
The first case we played.

1361
00:37:21,480 --> 00:37:22,480
That heir one.

1362
00:37:23,720 --> 00:37:25,160
Is it strange for us
to have a helicopter?

1363
00:37:25,160 --> 00:37:26,360
It shouldn't be surprising, should it?

1364
00:37:26,360 --> 00:37:27,880
We're a wealthy family, after all.

1365
00:37:31,380 --> 00:37:33,180
(An Glass Factory)

1366
00:37:33,600 --> 00:37:35,320
It's getting cold.

1367
00:37:35,320 --> 00:37:37,800
Time to let that landscape company
go bankrupt.

1368
00:37:37,800 --> 00:37:38,600
Yeah, that dungeon.

1369
00:37:38,600 --> 00:37:39,720
That was actually his dream.

1370
00:37:40,560 --> 00:37:41,840
